#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:4
msgid ""
"You are the Hero routing agent. The user has described what they want to "
"do in natural language. Your job is to figure out which Hero workflow is "
"the best fit and either run it directly or suggest it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:6
msgid "Available workflows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:8
msgid "Agent-powered workflows (slash commands)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:9
msgid ""
"**/design** — Design a feature, enhancement, or platform change. Produces"
" a spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:10
msgid "**/diagnose** — Investigate a bug, find root cause, produce a fix spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:11
msgid "**/deliver** — Execute an approved spec — implement, test, and complete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:12
msgid ""
"**/review** — Review code, PRs, security posture, or architecture "
"decisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:13
msgid ""
"**/compose** — Break a large initiative into sequenced specs with a "
"delivery plan."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:14
msgid "**/convention** — Document a codebase pattern as a convention spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:15
msgid "**/decide** — Evaluate an architectural decision with structured analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:16
msgid ""
"**/discover** — Explore product direction, brainstorm features, and "
"prioritize."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:17
msgid "**/docs** — Create or update technical documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:18
msgid "**/release** — Assess release readiness and deployment risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:19
msgid "**/retro** — Post-delivery retrospective comparing spec vs actual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:20
msgid "**/note** — Capture conversation or thinking as a note."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:21
msgid "**/scan** — Analyze codebase stack and generate knowledge base entries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:22
msgid "**/check** — Run workspace health check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:24
msgid "CLI commands (run in terminal)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:25
msgid "`hero status` / `hero dashboard` — See workspace state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:26
msgid "`hero search <query>` — Find specs by keyword."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:27
msgid "`hero search` — Browse knowledge base entries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:28
msgid "`hero spec new <slug>` — Scaffold a new spec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:29
msgid "`hero scan` — Detect tech stack and generate knowledge stubs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:30
msgid "`hero check` — Health check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:31
msgid "`hero note <slug>` — Quick note capture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:32
msgid ""
"`hero do <request>` — Route natural language (CLI version of this "
"command)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:34
msgid "Routing logic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:36
msgid "Read the user's request: `$ARGUMENTS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:37
msgid "Identify the intent:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:38
msgid "**Bug/error/broken/fix** → `/diagnose`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:39
msgid "**New feature/build/design/add** → `/design`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:40
msgid "**Implement/deliver/ship/code** → `/deliver`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:41
msgid "**Review/PR/pull request** → `/review`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:42
msgid "**Break down/decompose/epic/plan** → `/compose`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:43
msgid "**Convention/pattern/standard** → `/convention`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:44
msgid "**Decision/tradeoff/compare/choose** → `/decide`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:45
msgid "**Explore/brainstorm/roadmap** → `/discover`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:46
msgid "**Document/docs/explain** → `/docs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:47
msgid "**Release/deploy/version** → `/release`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:48
msgid "**Retro/postmortem/lessons** → `/retro`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:49
msgid "**Note/capture/remember** → `/note`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:50
msgid "**Scan/detect/onboard/stack** → `/scan`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:51
msgid "**Check/health/validate** → `/check`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:52
msgid "**Status/dashboard/overview** → suggest `hero dashboard`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:53
msgid "**Search/find/look up** → suggest `hero search <query>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:54
msgid ""
"If the intent is clear, run the matching slash command directly, passing "
"through any relevant context from the user's request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:55
msgid ""
"If the intent is ambiguous, present the top 2-3 options and ask the user "
"to choose."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:56
msgid ""
"If no match is found, list the available workflows and ask the user to "
"clarify."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:58
msgid "Important"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:60
msgid ""
"When routing to a slash command, pass the user's original context as "
"arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:61
msgid "Do NOT just echo back the command — actually run the workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:62
msgid ""
"If the user's request includes a specific spec slug or file path, include"
" it when routing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/hero.md:64
msgid "User request: $ARGUMENTS"
msgstr ""

